From 7218de733ca2dac9f0367a008162db13c6716158 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:58:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Add an in-app Help topic for the RF Propagation Monitor

Add "RF Propagation Monitor" to the Radio group of the bundled guide:
what the monitor observes, how to open it, the 24-hour learning period
and 14/30/60-day baseline, states and colours, evidence used, settings
under Settings > Notifications > RF propagation monitor, and limits
(RX log firmware, false alerts, experimental thresholds). Labels match
propagation-ui.js and radio-page-ui.js.

help-screenshots.cjs now also captures the monitor panel from a
synthetic baseline and unusual window injected into the isolated page
(help-assets/propagation.png, 256-colour palette, 36.8 KB; demonstration
keys only, no map tiles). The native Help test expects 22 topics.

help-assets/propagation.png must be added to package.json build.files
next to the other help-assets entries before packaging.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019jwdUNLdgFDTkdkrPTAK1B
