From 9bf0d002999085337b31fb34a23c5b32cdb4fd80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:58:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Show radio-reported packet counters in Radio Health

Radio Health now has a Radio counters section built from the stats the
radio already returns during synchronization (CMD_GET_STATS subtypes
0-2): packets sent and received since radio start, raw TX/RX airtime
and uptime values, and when the counters were read. Firmware without
statistics (protocol below 8, or statistics disabled after an error)
shows "Unavailable on this firmware". No additional radio commands are
sent; values update on synchronization and Refresh radio data.

Packet counters were physically observed incrementing per transmission
(releases/0.8.22-rc.43.md). Airtime and uptime units are not documented
in this repository, so they are labelled as raw radio values.

The propagation acceptance plan's passive-operation step now uses
Packets sent from Radio Health. Adds a unit test and
radio-counters.browser.test.cjs (synthetic events only).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019jwdUNLdgFDTkdkrPTAK1B
