 - Show radio-reported counters in Radio Health: packets sent and received since radio start, raw TX/RX airtime and uptime values, and when they were read; firmware without radio statistics shows Unavailable. No additional radio commands. Synthetic tests only.
 
+- Show the expected SHA-256 for an available update when the GitHub asset digest and the release SHA256SUMS.txt agree, with copy buttons and the PowerShell Get-FileHash command; warn and withhold the download link when they disagree, and warn when either is missing. Nightlink still opens downloads in the browser and does not hash the downloaded file.
+
 - Add a passive RF Propagation Monitor: a header indicator, a Radio > Observe & diagnose panel with evidence, trend, observations and event history, and settings under Settings > Notifications. It compares received packets with a per-radio local baseline and reports "Possible RF opening" or "Strong RF anomaly" with hysteresis and cooldown. It never transmits, enables RX logging or uses the network, and does not claim an atmospheric cause. Thresholds are untested hypotheses; synthetic tests only.
 
 ## 0.8.26 — 2026-10-31
diff --git a/UPDATES.md b/UPDATES.md
index 086f48b..52224a6 100644
--- a/UPDATES.md
+++ b/UPDATES.md
@@ -6,6 +6,8 @@ The Windows client reads the public GitHub latest-release API (`https://api.gith
 
 An available update opens its GitHub download in the browser. Nightlink does not download or install executables automatically, restart itself, or disconnect a radio during a check. Quit Nightlink cleanly before running an installer. Existing installed clients retain the update behavior in their installed version.
 
+Checksum check (0.8.27 candidates and later): when an update is available, Nightlink also reads `SHA256SUMS.txt` from the same release. It accepts only the exact release download URL for this repository and tag, follows a redirect only to GitHub release storage (`objects.githubusercontent.com` or `release-assets.githubusercontent.com`) over HTTPS, caps the file at 16 KB, times out after 10 seconds and rejects malformed lines. The expected SHA-256 is shown only when the GitHub asset digest and `SHA256SUMS.txt` agree. Settings > Data & updates then shows the file name, the expected SHA-256, copy buttons and the PowerShell command `Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 "$env:USERPROFILE\Downloads\<file>"`. Nightlink opens the download in the browser and cannot hash the downloaded file itself; comparing the values is the user's step. If the two published values disagree, Nightlink shows a warning, hides Open download and opens the release page instead. If a value is missing or cannot be read, it shows a warning and no expected checksum.
+
 Installed candidate versions are compared against stable versions in rc.33 and later: a stable release of the same version is newer than its candidate, while a candidate with a higher base version is ahead of an older stable release. Candidates are not offered by the stable update feed. Local candidate files do not become remote updates until an approved release is published.
 
 Repository visibility was changed to public at the owner's request on 2026-10-25. The public feed and full downloads of both v0.8.19 Windows artifacts were verified without authentication, including matching GitHub SHA-256 digests. This confirms distribution and download access, not successful installation on every client. No new stable release was published as part of this verification.
